id: pm-0p4aal
title: Fail the required coverage aggregate when any shard fails or is skipped
description: "CI run39077888907 reported Coverage shard3/4 FAILURE and the required Gates (coverage) SKIPPED. The protected check set requires the aggregate but not individual shards. A default dependent-job skip can therefore satisfy the required coverage context without a successful test run. Run the aggregate unconditionally after dependencies settle and explicitly require a successful shard matrix before checkout, report merge or upload."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-17T23:47:36.828Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-18T01:25:33.433Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-18T01:25:32.474Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-18T01:25:32.474Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 30
acceptance_criteria: "Reproduce missing unconditional aggregate admission before the change; Require successful shard result before report merging; Exercise success, failure, skipped and canceled matrix outcomes; Preserve every shard, exact full coverage thresholds, existing permissions and free hosted features"
goal: project management = context management
objective: Keep required verification receipts truthful across sharded execution
value: A failed or absent test cohort cannot be mistaken for completed coverage admission
why_now: "The current SDK delivery produced a real failed shard and skipped aggregate, exposing the existing hosted enforcement gap."
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: low
confidence: 100
resolution: "Always run the required coverage aggregate, explicitly reject unsuccessful shard outcomes, and require successful admission before report merging or pinned Codecov verification. Align both workflow contract suites, retaining checksum verification, immutable references, exact-head uploads, failure diagnostics and quiet logs."
expected_result: "Failed, canceled, skipped or missing shards fail the required coverage context; successful shards retain verified exact-head reports and threshold-failure diagnostics."
actual_result: "Run39084972483 demonstrated the required aggregate correctly failing instead of being skipped. Its one stale Codecov condition assertion is corrected. All24 tests across both contract suites pass, plus the linked five-input admission control. Repository docstring quality passes after documenting four workflow helpers. Final revised-head hosted coverage remains mandatory; no thresholds, permissions, paid features or production runtime changed in this revision."
