comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-17T23:47:36.828Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete all-status full keyword-AND reads returned126 coverage-shard and389 coverage-skipped records with zero payload omissions. Read the completed exact-count authority, nightly job-budget and PR-readiness owners with full metadata/history. They shipped integer-count enforcement, bounded nightly execution and watch receipts respectively; this new defect is the required CI aggregate producer being skipped. Reuse the current CI capability parent and preserve those completed deliveries. GitHub documentation explicitly identifies failed-dependency skips as potentially nonblocking and recommends always() with needs for required aggregate jobs: https://docs.github.com/en/pull-requests/how-tos/merge-and-close-pull-requests/troubleshooting-required-status-checks"
  "2026-10-17T23:57:55.613Z","harness:codex","The new contract failed on the original missing job-level always() condition. The corrected workflow runs the required aggregate after shard completion and first executes a real shell guard over success/failure/cancelled/skipped/empty results; only success passes. Failed admission skips checkout and merging; artifact upload and Codecov verification are explicitly gated on admission. Threshold-failure diagnostics remain available after successful admission. All21 workflow contracts pass in the230-test corrected cohort, and workflow permissions remain unchanged/read-only by default."
  "2026-10-18T01:24:52.712Z","harness:codex","Final-head run39084972483 proves the aggregate now fails on an unsuccessful shard instead of being skipped. Its sole failing test is the existing pinned Codecov bootstrap contract, which still expects the old unconditional !cancelled() verifier. Updated that coupled expectation to require successful shard admission while retaining checksum verification, immutable pins, exact-head uploads and quiet logs. Added concise documentation to four workflow assertion helpers in response to the reviewer documentation-coverage warning. The reviewer requested splitting other scopes, but this delivery retains the connected SDK, consumer qualification, CI and eligible dependency work explicitly requested together in one PR. CodeRabbit reported no new actionable code comments for 9fc5031; optional review providers remain unavailable, and required DeepScan remains pending. Only this coverage-contract item is reopened and claimed for these edits."
